A||||60||sjp777||I hate SUV's and minivans||||13||
Z||000000||sjp777||05-19-2001||11:48 PM||||Has anyone else noticed that the SUV/minivan craze has turned the American road into a grazing land for herds of big go-nowhere-fast mobile traffic impediments?<P>Please just get the f**k out of my way. My car doesn't need to come to a full stop to make a right hand turn, and I can reach highway speed BEFORE I try to merge onto the highway.<P>And stop burning the hair off the back of my head with your headlights.<BR>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_2.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A><P><p>[This message has been edited by sjp777 (edited 05-20-2001).]||||reg||13
Z||000001||danny boy||05-20-2001||12:37 AM|||| Amen, brother.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||05-20-2001||01:23 AM||||The part about not reaching highway speed is what ticks me off the most. I hate having to merge onto a 65 mph highway going 30 mph because the guy in front of you won't step on it. <P>Than you have to floor it or get rear ended.<P>The silky smooth 32 valve 4.7-liter v8 in this Truck has more passing power than my 2.8-liter v6 formula does. I don't have to stop to take a right turn either. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Front_of_Tundra_truck_1.jpg"> <BR> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 05-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||fropuff||05-20-2001||01:25 AM||||...And quit wasting our oil supply with filling your vehicles up with gas only to drive yourself to go shopping!  And quit trying to race across the highway instead of waiting 5 more seconds until I pass!  And quit rolling the damn things over!<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters rock!||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||05-20-2001||06:52 AM||||First, I do have to stand up a little for minivans, they actually do serve a purpose and they fit in a garage. They are great for hauling stuff like Fiero parts or in my case in the future the whole thing. SUVs on the other hand have no purpose at least on the road. They evolved from an off road vehicle and should have stayed there. Im trying to figure out why a 17 yo girl for example needs a 3 ton truck ...yes truck, thats what they are......to just haul her butt to the mall or school. The biggest argument they have is that they sit higher up and they dont feel so intimidated with other cars.They have this misconception that there really luxury sports cars in disquise and thats how there usually driven. Its still a GD pickup truck with some extra seats and a price tag comparable to a loaded Lincoln or Caddy-talk about stupid buyers. Before all the gals jump in, its not just them. Most of the guys that have them are swept over too by the mentality that 'hey, im macho and I can do anything I want'. Well im for keeping them off the road as daily transportation. Leave em for the off roading, boat hauling, hunter/fishermen like their supposed to be.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fierowrecker||05-20-2001||09:01 AM||||I like your comment about teen girls driving SUV's...<BR>Here in southwest Michigan, many people found out how well they protect school kids...<BR>Seems a set of twin girls were going to a highschool event and turned into the path of an oncoming semi, the driver of the semi didn't have time to react, and took out the SUV and killed one of the twins...<BR>The driver of the SUV survived, and now needs to live with the fact that she killed her sister...<BR>All SUV drivers that have a macho mentallity of invulnerabillity should have seen that wreck, It looked like hamburger...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||hugh||05-20-2001||09:13 AM||||First,I don't like SUV's.Now let's get something straight.It's the mentality of the driver,not the car.I bought my wife a minivan last year.It has a 3.3v6 and with me driving is as competitive(for want of a better word)as any car on the road from a stop light.When I leave the entrance ramp,I usually am over the speed limit so no one slows down for me.Wasting gas,I don't think so.I drove to Connecticut Easter weekend with 3 people in it,the air on,at 70MPH I averaged over 19 MPG.I prefer my wife use the car for shopping,it's easier than walking with her arms full of groceries.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||05-20-2001||09:26 AM||||well, uh, i own a '98 Jeep Cherokee and my fiance' has a '97 Honda Passport.<P>i like my Jeep, it has loads of power... if i could put that straight 6 in the GT it would be awesome!<P>neither of the <I>trucks</I> have rolled over on us yet, nor did we buy them for the feeling of invinceability!  he bought them because they are extreemly convienent (and i would sooner loose <B>both</B> my teste's than own a minivan!  <P>suv's are great for going on trips to football games (as much as i have tried you cannot (repeat cannot) have a serious tailgate party with a fiero... there's just no place to put the grill!), and hauling mountain bikes around in.  also, i can put the dogs in the back of the suv, and keep the GT hair free!<P>now having said that, there are a lot of people on the road that behave like idiots behind the wheel of these things (and especially in minivans!).  and their are a lot of rich 16 yo spoiled little girls driving around in new 4 runners and Pathfinders (something i completely disagree with... i think everyone should have a junker for their first car (even for if it's for just 6 months)). <P>there are also a lot of idiot drivers that own taurus's and camera's and camry's and xxxxx.  i think they just need to improve the driver training and penalty system in this country, and once they do that the world will be a better place again!<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||hugh||05-20-2001||09:56 AM||||HOOP,Let me repeat!It is the mentality of the driver,not the vehicle they are driving!I don't like SUV's,like I don't like lots of things,such as some colors,tastes,jobs,etc.It has nothing to do with the vehicle itself.The problem with SUV's as determined by (I think)Consumer reports or a similar organization is the perception you think are going slower than you actually are in a SUV.That contributes greatly to rollovers. My minivan can do all the things your SUV can do and is easier to get into for my wife because she is only 4'10".That part about"especially in minivans" bothers me.I hope it wasn't directed at me.As far as both your testes,I'd rather drive a 49 Studebaker with only 3 wheels on a superhighway in the passing lane than do that.||||reg||1
Z||000009||firstfiero||05-20-2001||11:19 AM||||    #1) I avoid driving my suv like the plague. It's my wifes car and I hate it. If I'm not sitting two inches of the ground I'm not interested.<BR>    #2) I understand a mini van is usefull...that being said I would rather swallow the end of a gun then be seen in one or worse have to use one as my daily driver!<BR>   #3) Their is an exception to every rule and that is the bmw. The x5 will out handle us in the twisties and suck our doors off in the straight away. Damn I miss my old 5 series....<P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">         <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000010||bHooper||05-20-2001||12:03 PM||||hugh, no it wasn't directed at you.  i think if people know anything about me, they know i'm not a flamer.  sure i may get pissed off at the people who come here to dump some car off for more money that 4 of them are worth, but other than that i try to always keep good humor about things.<P>as for the minivan thing, whot you do not know (of course never having seen my car in person you wouldn't know this anyway) is that i had a minivan run me off of the highway... into the grassy median (at 60 mph), once.  needless to say, it tainted me a little bit.<P>actually, i have become very impressed with the handling of my Cherokee.  it is very sporty, for a truck. sure, it's not the GT, but it ain't yoiur fathers olds either! <P>as for the testicle thingy, i would expect a Bugatti type 35 as restitution.  then and only then would i be satisfied   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000011||PBJ||05-20-2001||12:14 PM||||NO kidding about the burning the hair off the back of the neck with the headlights. I can tilt the rear view mirror inside but that blinding glare from the dr outside mirror.||||reg||1
Z||000012||wkayl||05-20-2001||01:43 PM||||I own a 2001 Chev Silverado 4x4 ext cab short-bed.  My wife drives it to work every day.  The reason we own it is to pull a 16 ft travel trailer.  I don't think having a $30,000 truck just sit would very worthwhile.  She put over 300 miles on the last tank of gas (city driving)and got 15.5 mpg.  My Fiero doesn't get much better than that in city driving.  As for the headlights in the rear view mirror, I went to a salvage yard and picked up an auto dimming mirror with temp and compass from a 2000 Silverado ($50) and put it in my Fiero.  Now when those "big nasty 4x4 suvs" pull up behind me it doesn't blind me.  Here in Colorado the worst drivers on the road are females (not to pick on women, but 70% of cars I see pulled over are female)or young guys in Hondas, Saturns, etc... cutting in and out of traffic.<P>My feeling is if you want to drive a ricer, drive a ricer.  If you want to drive an suv, drive an suv.  If you want to drive a cool Fiero, drive a cool Fiero.<P>Last time I checked, it was a mostly free country (but that could be a whole nother thread).<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||rockcrawl||05-20-2001||03:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Last time I checked, it was a mostly free country<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Right on!<P> I don't own a minivan or an SUV, but I don't hate people who do. I drive a 3/4 ton van 5 days a week for work (30,000 miles/year). The most annoying thing is the drivers with the "Please just get the f**k out of my way" mentality.||||reg||1
Z||000014||sjp777||05-20-2001||04:05 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rockcrawl:<BR><B> Right on!<P> I don't own a minivan or an SUV, but I don't hate people who do. I drive a 3/4 ton van 5 days a week for work (30,000 miles/year). The most annoying thing is the drivers with the "Please just get the f**k out of my way" mentality.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You obviously are exactly one of the ones I was referring to<P>And I don't remember saying anything about hating people who own them. I said I hate those types of vehicles.<P>My parents have an Explorer. I certainly don't hate them for it, I just don't want them anywhere near me on the road.<p>[This message has been edited by sjp777 (edited 05-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||sqoach||05-21-2001||12:59 AM||||I don't like all the big scary stationwagons-with-lift-kits thinking they can just cut me off because I'm an ant. There's a lot of younger people here with SUV's with four 15s in the back bumping along and not paying attention at all. That really annoys me. And they get right up behind me and act like they're gonna run over the top of me. The lights don't bother me though. That's what tinting the back window is for  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>But, I don't hate SUV's. Some of them are pretty nice, and I'm sure they come in handy for what they're intended to be used for. I actually like the looks of the Jeep Grand Cherokee and the new Chevy TrailBlazer. There's good points and bad points for everything. Just drive your Fiero and be happy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||9
Z||000016||camaro2fiero||05-21-2001||01:50 AM||||Well when it comes to SUVs and Minivans,they have thier purpose.I too seem to find that some drivers of the vehicles do tend to feel invinciable.Then again I feel like a little speed demon in my 84 coupe,lol.I just think that people nowadays are not thinking clearly when they get behind the wheel.More people on the roads = more idiots too. I have had problems with people not seeing me when they change lanes.Either they dont look carefully or they think they are invincable.I seem to have become more cautious now. I personally dont like either vehicle in question. I think they scarf the gas , you can say all you want about the gas mileage in comparison to the Fiero.IT AINT THE SAME.Drive a Tahoe or Expedition full out and you aint gittin no 19 MPG.My girlfriends gets 18 in the city without kicking down the motor.Anyways nothing personal just how I see it.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Neverfinished||05-21-2001||05:21 AM||||After around 20 near collisions with SUVs and the burning of my neck hair I have much hate towards them. My cherokee has alot of power but I get nervous even going around a curve in it. When an SUV tailgates me... which is often, just spike your brakes for a quick sec and that will get their attention... works like a charm||||reg||1
Z||000018||Raydar||05-21-2001||10:25 AM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Neverfinished:<BR><B>When an SUV tailgates me... which is often, just spike your brakes for a quick sec and that will get their attention... works like a charm</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not in Atlanta. Just pisses 'em off. <BR>I've thought about tossing an empty Coke can out of my sunroof, and bouncing it off their hood.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>If they report me, I'll just ask "How close were they if I could actually <I>do</I> that?" <P>I still think that some sympathetic D.A. or police officer ought to start charging tailgating SUV drivers with "Assault with a Motor Vehicle" if they hit a smaller car from behind. Start making examples of these morons. <P>BTW... <BR>I know that the term "SUV" conjures up images of Explorers, Expeditions, and such, but my wife has a Jeep Wrangler. It's an absolute blast to drive. Can almost make a U-turn in it's own length. It will fit in a parking space that even my Fiero will have to pass up. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 05-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||wkayl||05-21-2001||10:31 AM||||Like I said above, I have a full size 4x4, but....  It seems like everyone (not just SUVs) like to tailgate the Fiero.  And as Neverfinished said, a quick stomp on the brakes gets their attention.  They then flip you off and to get them really pi**ed, I just smile when the hot rod by.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000020||Greg Piet||05-21-2001||01:52 PM||||I guess I am a bit more practical...<BR>I dont like tall SUV's b/c many tennage drivers who dont check their mirrors like to switch lanes and try to crunch my Fiero.<P>If I had the ability I would have everyone (myself included) driving little tiny cars getting 60mpg.  This way I could save my Fiero for "special" events and use much less gasoline.  I used to ride a motorcycle most places getting 50 mpg and that was not too bad, but in the city I got in too many near misses with 4 wheel vehicles.  Before it comes into question I was not squeezing between cars, going between lanes, or doing other things that some motorcyclers do that are reckless.<P>If I am in error on the following I apologize, but I believe that most cars on the road have only one occupant, and is not hauling excessive cargo.  I do not see why someone needs an Expedition as a daily commute vehicle.||||reg||1
Z||000021||Fiero5||05-21-2001||02:18 PM||||SUV drivers are slackers!<P>I like it when there is a heard of them on the highway in one section, and I zip in and around them like their driving pylons, heh, heh.<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero1sig.JPG">                   <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||12
Z||000022||88formula||05-21-2001||05:37 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Tundra_behind_FIERO.JPG"> <BR>Get out of my way or I'll run you over. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000023||FieroLisa||05-21-2001||05:48 PM||||I don't like jack@sses who drive SUVs either...but there are also jack@sses who drive Fieros. <P>OK SO here's the argument people seem to present: SUVs belong off-road they are too big, too slow, waste of gas.<P>But on the other side, Do you own a Fiero to go 140 mph?? I sure don't. I enjoy it because its the vehicle of my choice. Does that mean an SUV driver HAS to go offroad with his? No, its his vehicle of choice.<P>Granted, an SUV will do more damage in a head on collision than our Fieros, but in a lot of cases, although of course not all, the driver of the Fiero/Camaro/Z/Fill-in-the-blank with any sports car, We will most likely speed more and take more chances driving around those curves that your supposed to go 35mph around... But you want to try it at 60 just cause you can- who's to say theres not another car or a kid riding their bike?<P>I'm not saying everyone speeds or corners like a madman- But not all SUV drivers drive stupid either.<P>And as for polluting the air? Well we take off our catalytic converters just for the good sound it makes (and no I'm not flaming those who do it, I plan to soon)<P>So there's my $ .02 which was probably more like $20 but keep in mind, we are not perfect or invincible nor are we the only cars that should be on the road.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT: 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air intake<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>       <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48495967&Sequence=0&res=high"> ||||reg||1
Z||000024||SteveJ||05-21-2001||06:17 PM||||Ever drive into a parking lot and park nose to nose with one of those big SUV's? What do you think would happen of it hit you on the road?||||reg||1
Z||000025||Fierowrecker||05-21-2001||06:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SteveJ:<BR><B>Ever drive into a parking lot and park nose to nose with one of those big SUV's? What do you think would happen of it hit you on the road?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I know what happens on a rain slicked road when an SUV slams on it's brakes to let another driver into his lane...<BR>Lost my hood, and got a ticket for following too close (4 car lengths!!!)...<BR>Then the damn insurance company writes it off as totalled!!!<BR>Fixed and painted at my expense...<BR>Need to carry a nine MM and a 45 cal...<BR>If the nine don't stop em, the 45 will!!!<BR>Gotta have the metric gun for foreign vehicals...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000026||FieroLisa||05-21-2001||07:55 PM||||SteveJ- but the thing is, Trucks are more or less the same size, if not bigger, and I have one to pull my horse trailer. Conversion Vans- same size. Trucks from Utility companies, same size. <P>I'm not saying some SUV drivers aren't idiots, but there are a ton of people who drive SUVs who are fine, and tons of people who drive other vehicles who need to be off the road entirely.||||reg||1
Z||000027||SteveJ||05-21-2001||08:12 PM||||Pulling a trailer, no problem. Pickup trucks, well we give 'em the benefit of the doubt, they use it for business. But I think a lot of us see those SUV's being used just to cart someone to the market and back.<P>Wrong attitude for the owner of a small car I know.||||reg||1
