Z||000035||stsmithgt||05-22-2001||04:56 PM||||Hey Hoop!  I have a Colt 45. I bought some jacketed hollow points that about swallow up a 9mm slug.  There is a difference.  That's why 45 hollow points are called, "flying ash cans".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I'm glad I've never had to use it on anybody.  It's pretty destructive.  You ought to have seen what it did to a big ol' snapping turtle when I was back in Arkansas.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000036||DRH||05-22-2001||05:09 PM||||9mm is pretty close to a 38 in size. Not sure if they can be used interchangeably though...<P>Funny how this turned to guns. They do have something in common. Just remember; "SUVs don't kill people, people kill people."  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000037||stsmithgt||05-22-2001||05:49 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fact45acp&9mm.jpg">   Found these on a page.  Not the greatest pics, but close enough.  Another page had some 9mm with a .364 diameter while the 45. was a .451.... It didn't say who's ruler they were using so it's only a numbers comparison.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  My Fiero is buddies with my 45. (had to fit Fiero in there somehow.) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/coltlogo.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 05-22-2001).]||||reg||1
