Z||000039||LarryB||05-23-2001||09:56 AM||||A 9MM Parabellum has a bullet diameter of .355".<BR>A .38 Special has a bullet diameter of .357". (A .357 magnum is essentially a .38 case lengthened slightly so some knucklehead doesn't try to chamber it in a .38)<P>It would be possible to use a 9mm bullet in a .38 case but the accuracy probably wouldn't be worth a goldurn and I don't think I'd want to use one in a +P or .357 handload. <P>As for SUV's, I've got one.  As to why..that's MY business. NOT anyone else's. <BR>If you've got a problem with them, its YOUR problem. Deal with it. <BR>||||reg||1
