Z||000041||88 Fiero||05-23-2001||10:44 AM||||88 Formula I agree with you. Japanese cars seems to be much better built than american cars. I dont mean to bash american cars. I love them but when it comes to reliability for some reason japanese cars stands out. I own a 2000 4Runner which I just hook up a S/C unit on it. I love the extra power but not that stupid to race it. My brother got a 2000 Tundra and I'll tell you what that truck got alot of balls. 32valve V8 sures knows how to harass a couple of F150's and Silverado's. ||||reg||1
Z||000042||sjp777||05-23-2001||11:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LarryB:<BR><B>A 9MM Parabellum has a bullet diameter of .355".<BR>A .38 Special has a bullet diameter of .357". (A .357 magnum is essentially a .38 case lengthened slightly so some knucklehead doesn't try to chamber it in a .38)<P>It would be possible to use a 9mm bullet in a .38 case but the accuracy probably wouldn't be worth a goldurn and I don't think I'd want to use one in a +P or .357 handload. <P>As for SUV's, I've got one.  As to why..that's MY business. NOT anyone else's. <BR>If you've got a problem with them, its YOUR problem. Deal with it. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Shouldn't you be out in the driveway putting a fresh NRA sticker in the back window of your truck or something?<P>||||reg||13
Z||000043||mshill||05-23-2001||12:15 PM||||Oh youth...  You guys wait till you have four kids and tell me you won't own a minivan.  My wife thinks Suburbans and Expeditions are too big, so she drives a GMC Safari with the old 4.3L HO engine.  Nice van, good power, even pulls my 18ft boat up the hill to Tahoe or where ever.  I have three Fieros, the Safari and a POS Taurus.  Can't wait till the Taurus dies so I can get a truck.  It's not the car/van/SUV, it's the drivers. ||||reg||1
Z||000044||ThatRickGuy||05-23-2001||12:29 PM||||I'm of the firm beleif that there are no stupid cars, only stupid drivers. And for some reason a lot of stupid drivers wind up in large vehicles. I live just south of DC, and drive into the city every weekend for a night club job I have. and the drivers out here are insane, I'm used to getting cut off and tail gated, it doesn't bother me so much any more, except when it's a large vehicle. If you're going to tailgate someone, make sure your breaking distance is less then theirs! As for the emissions, SUVs are classified differently then passanger cars (light/heavy duty truck) as such they have looser emmission requirements, so even at the same MPG they are putting out more 'bad gas'. And last but not least, anyone who has mentioned an extreme dislike for minivans, claiming them to be week and pansy... go here: <A HREF="http://webpages.krausonline.com/spaul/" TARGET=_blank>http://webpages.krausonline.com/spaul/</A> <BR>||||reg||1
